Changes to subopt-kaks

2.0.0 (2026-11-06)

 Behaviour changes relative to 1.0.0 (read before comparing with old runs)
  * yn00_cds_optimal / the C aligners: optimal alignments could end one
    residue early (wrong stride decoding the best cell). dN/dS from
    unaligned CDS can therefore differ from 1.0.0 output; the bundled
    test pair now matches its pre-aligned reference exactly.
  * --gapopen / --gapext are always penalties; 1.0.0 turned them into a
    gap bonus for any sign given.
  * Default substitution matrix is BLOSUM62 (BLOSUM50 was never shipped).
  * --minlen is now applied by the Zuker tools (it was parsed and ignored).
  * kaks --genetic-code takes the NCBI transl_table id (1 = standard,
    2 = vertebrate mitochondrial, ...); the earlier 0-5 PAML numbering is
    gone and 0 is rejected.
  * kaks yn00 with more than two sequences uses per-pair F3x4 codon
    frequencies, as PAML yn00 does; --common-f3x4 restores the pooled
    frequencies used by the C tools. Two-sequence results are unchanged.
  * License is GNU GPL v3 or later (the Rust crate previously said MIT).

 kaks (rust/subopt-kaks), version 2.0.0
  Pairwise maximum-likelihood dN/dS under the Goldman & Yang 1994 codon
  model (--method ml, --codon-freq fequal|f1x4|f3x4|fcodon), a port of
  PAML codeml runmode = -2, validated pair by pair against codeml and
  yn00 on PAML's example data under 11 genetic codes: 3970 comparisons,
  3 differences, all explained (tst/paml_compare/README.md).
  All 27 NCBI genetic codes (--genetic-code, --list-codes).
  Library crate plus CLI. WebAssembly: WASI command line (make wasi) and
  a browser page with batch upload of many alignment files (make web;
  https://hyphaltip.github.io/subopt-kaks/, deployed by GitHub Actions).
  Makefile install targets (make install PREFIX=|BINDIR=|DESTDIR=).

 C tools
  build
   Top-level Makefile: `make` configures and builds squid then src;
   `make test`, `make install [PREFIX=...]` (installs matrices and man
   pages, compiles the data directory into the binaries), `make rust`.
   Links with GCC >= 10 (duplicate global `noisy` removed).
   tst/run_tests.sh + tst/expected: byte-for-byte regression tests.

  zuker.c
   optimal_align decoded the best-cell index with the wrong stride, so the
   local/global optimal alignment could end one residue early. The test
   pair now gives the same dN/dS as the pre-aligned reference.
   Global alignments now always trace back from the bottom-right cell.
   seq2 matrix indices computed once per column instead of once per cell.
   All error paths free their matrices; reverse_seq copies are freed.

  all aligners
   --gapopen/--gapext were negated to a positive bonus; now always a
   penalty regardless of the sign given.
   Uninitialised file handles / counters on early exits fixed
   (cds_zuker_align crashed in fputc). --output - means stdout.
   Default matrix BLOSUM62 (BLOSUM50 is not shipped); --matrix accepts a
   bare name resolved through --matrix-dir, $SUBOPT_MATRIX_DIR, $SUBOPTDIR,
   ./matricies/aa, ../matricies/aa, or the compiled-in data directory.

  zuker_align.c
   cds_seqs[cdsct++] wrote past the end of the 2-element array.

  yn00_cds_optimal.c
   Multiple input files no longer leak or mis-size the sequence arrays.

  yn00_cds_prealigned.c
   Header printed once, not once per input file; per-MSA memory freed.

  yn00_simple.c
   GetFreqs failure now frees its buffers and resets PAML state.

 packaging
  Top-level Makefile builds squid and the C tools; make test, make install.
  GNU GPL v3 or later throughout (LICENSE, Cargo.toml, READMEs).
  Man pages: placeholders filled in, contact email updated.
  Perl helper scripts take options instead of hardcoded paths.

1.0.0 (2019-01-23)
 GitHub release of the original C tools (no Changelog entry was written).

0.06 
 yn00_cds_prealigned.c 
  a new program which will process multiple alignments and calculate all
  pairwise combination as the PAML yn00 does, will also accept multiple
  sequence files to process on the cmd line.

 squid/phylip.c
  modified to support really parsing multiple MSA alignments in a single file

 yn00_cds_optimal.c
  Will calculate alignments and dN, dS for all pairwise combinations not 
  just the first two sequences in the file.

  Also remove last codon of a sequence if it is a stop codon.

 
0.05 
 zuker.c  
  boundary condition error fixed in fill_matrix - should be offsetting
  location of best_loc by doing i-1

 yn00_cds_optimal.c 
  fixed bug which was caused by extra increment in cds_seq 

0.04 
 yn00_simple.c  
  Allow skipping of codons which contain a non-DNA char 
  (ambiguity bases or an N) so that can still calculate a distance value
  while skipping the codons which contain the character
   
  err2 now prints to stderr so that redirection capture is not cluttered
   with error/debugging messages.

0.03
 * Support --noheader options in yn00_cds_optimal and yn00_zuker_align
